        {
          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Маршрутка: the most Ukrainian vehicle",
          "items": [
            "A **маршрутка** is a minibus that runs a fixed route but stops wherever a passenger asks, much like shared minibuses across Eastern Europe, Asia, and Latin America.",
            "To get off: **На зупинці, будь ласка!** (at the stop, please) or just **Зупиніть, будь ласка** (stop, please).",
            "You pay the driver, often by passing the money forward hand to hand. Passing on the money of the person behind you is normal, not an extraordinary courtesy.",
            "⚠️ The word *маршрутка* isn't in any tourist phrasebook, but it's the vehicle you'll ride most outside the city center."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sub",
          "text": "Travel phrases that cover most situations"
